  {
   "line": 4,
   "text": "Early in the chain sits the booster. It's a system: a rule that takes in one signal, one list of numbers, and gives back another. Its rule is one line of code: multiply every sample by four. But the chip after it can only store values from minus one to plus one. Hand it two, and it writes down one. That flattening is called clipping.",
   "clip": "/Users/cleiton.loiola/personal/lessons/dsp-oppenheim/01-signals-and-systems/4-video/vo-s110/line04.wav",
