  {
   "line": 11,
   "text": "So the fix is to keep every input inside the range. The loudest input the booster ever sees, speakerphones included, is point five. Times two lands right on the edge, with no margin. Instead, keep the loudest peak at point eight, a fifth below the edge. That gap is the headroom. Point eight divided by point five is one point six. Now the buzz meter, which measures the tones that weren't in the input, reads zero percent on every caller.",
